'''Lurando-Abyala''', sometimes collectively called the '''Algarves''' (predominately within [[Abyala]]), are a landmass comprising the totality of [[Lurandia]] and [[Abyala]]. When viewed as a single continent, Lurando-Abyala is the second largest continent by area after [[Fosia]] and the third largest continent by population. Lurando-Abyala make up most of the land in Adonia's [[Western Hemisphere]] and constitute the [[New World]].

Along with their [[Lists of islands of Lurando-Abyala|associated islands]], Lurando-Abyala cover x% of Adonia's total surface area and xx.x% of its land area. The topography is dominated by the [[Algarvean Cordillera]], a long chain of mountains that runs the length of the west coast of Abyala to the center of [[Lurandia]]. The flatter western side of the landmass is dominated by large river basins, such as the [[Marañón basin]], [[tba]]–[[tba]], [[tba]], and [[tba]] basins.

